/*
ListCreditPools The customer's scoped credit pools and what is left of each

Credit pools scoped to one or more meters and zero or more conditions on any dimension
the meters' events carry (`key = value`, `key in [values]`, `key not in [values]`). Usage
a pool's scope matches draws the pool before the plan's included allowance; the pool with
the most conditions draws first, then the one whose credit expires first. What no pool
covers, or what is left once the matching pools are empty, meets the included allowance
and then overage. A held pool (`spendable: false`) receives credit and is not drawn.

One entry per pool of each live subscription, for its current period: `available` is what
the pool held for the period, `drawn` what usage took so far, `remaining` what is left.
`accounts` splits what is left by kind of credit (`included@<pool>` from the plan,
forfeited when the subscription ends; `promotional@<pool>`; `purchased@<pool>`, kept).
`expiries` lists what is left per grant, soonest to expire first. Read a pool's movements
at `credit/movements?pool=included@<pool>`. A product-bound token sees its product's
subscriptions only.

A plan may set its own draw order: then only the pools it lists draw, in that order
(`draws: false` for the others), and the last may go negative (pay as you go). That pool
takes the usage it matches below zero instead of letting it reach the allowance; `balance`
is then below zero, and `pay_as_you_go` says what it owes: `negative` units, `due` (what they
come to at the meter's price, excl. VAT, billed on the next invoice as its own line), the
`cap` usage stops at with the reason `credit_limit_reached`, and `bought_credit`, the credit
the customer bought for the pool, which pays that line first, after VAT. `purchasable` says
whether the customer may buy credit for the pool (`POST credit/purchases` with `pool`).


 @param ctx context.Context - for authentication, logging, cancellation, deadlines, tracing, etc. Passed from http.Request or context.Background().
 @param org The organization id (the merchant platform's own tenant key).
 @return ApiListCreditPoolsRequest
*/
